<title>USA: Tele-Communications completes DMX merger.</title>
<headline>Tele-Communications completes DMX merger.</headline>
<dateline>ENGLEWOOD, Colo. 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tele-Communications Inc said Friday the merger between TCI Music Inc's subsidiary and DMX Inc was approved at a special meeting of DMX stockholders.</p>
<p>As a result of the merger, DMX became a wholly owned subsidiary of TCI Music and shares of DMX common stock will be exchanged for shares of TCI Music series A common stock. Affiliates of TCI own about 90 percent of the outstanding common shares, and about 98 percent of the voting power, of TCI Music.</p>
<p>TCI Music is managed by Liberty Media Corp, the programming unit of TCI.  Liberty Media has been an investor in DMX for a number of years.</p>
<p>TCI Music series A common stock is traded on the Nasdaq SmallCap Market under DMX's former symbol, TUNE.</p>
</text>
